    "sentence_translations": [
      "First-Year University Student",
      "",
      "Paul: Do you know? I saw a group of genius children today!",
      "",
      "Little Le: How do you know that they’re geniuses?",
      "",
      "Paul: Didn’t you tell me?",
      "That “Big 1” means “First-Year University Student”, and “Big 2” means “Second-Year University Student”.",
      "",
      "Little Le: Yes.",
      "",
      "Paul: I saw a group of children on the street today.",
      "Their teacher said “Big 1, walk on this side. Big 2, walk on that side.”",
      "You tell me, if they go to university when they’re that small, what are they if not geniuses?",
      "",
      "Little Le: Eh… Paul!",
      "Actually, kindergartens are divided into nursery, lower kindergarten, upper kindergarten and preschools.",
      "If a nursery has several classes, the kindergarten will divide them into “Nursery 1”, “Nursery 2”, “Nursery 3”.",
      "In the same way, if an upper kindergarten has several classes, they will be “Upper 1”, “Upper 2”…"
